    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193">

                <pb facs="0431" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-17T23:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 17, 1916, 11 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 18, 1 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3361. I have never been informed about your negotiations about <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi>, but (?) if there is delay, it is owing
                    to the fact that Germany is unwilling to admit obligation to pay indemnity,
                    while possibly willing to pay indemnity in this case. I have gathered this in
                    informal conversation with members of Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
